				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">nothing wrong wiht batwing wrapped trout. I would recommend some fresh herbs, like thyme and rosemary and a slice each of lime and lemon on the trout, with fresh cracked pepper and kosher sea salt of course. Wrap that in the bat wing and steam it in a bamboo steamer. I would make a creamy pepper sauce to serve over it, which is real simple. Take some cream, some whole peppercorns and a little fish or clam stock and reduce by about half, or to the thickness you like. I would also serve this with long grain rice, add some fresh parsley and cheese on the rice before service, a mild semi-soft cheese would be good. a few fresh veggies like asperagus, steamed or grilled and a bottle of Chardonney:)  BAM<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br />Priest of the Tribunal
